From 8d712b84937f1760a94c0636f771f48c85fbe487 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:32:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] player: expose decoded Dolby Vision RPU and enhancement type
 metadata

Read only existing decoded side data and explicit stream relations.
Keep new RST property definitions on one term line.
---
 DOCS/man/input.rst    | 27 ++++++++++++++++
 demux/demux_lavf.c    |  4 +++
 demux/demux_mkv.c     |  4 +++
 demux/dovi_split.c    |  4 +++
 demux/stheader.h      |  6 ++++
 player/command.c      | 50 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 video/dovi_metadata.h | 72 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 7 files changed, 167 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 video/dovi_metadata.h

diff --git a/DOCS/man/input.rst b/DOCS/man/input.rst
index 8970d5a..8c8ccd3 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/input.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/input.rst
@@ -3070,6 +3070,19 @@ Property list
     ``video-frame-info/repeat``
         Whether the frame must be delayed when decoding.
 
+    ``video-frame-info/dolby-vision-rpu-present``
+        Whether the current frame carries decoded Dolby Vision RPU metadata
+        or a non-empty raw RPU buffer. Includes its PTS-matched enhancement
+        layer when present. False does not prove the source file lacks RPUs:
+        a decoder or filter can omit side data. This does not report whether
+        the renderer applied the metadata.
+
+    ``video-frame-info/dolby-vision-el-type``
+        ``MEL`` or ``FEL``, identified from valid Profile 7 RPU header and
+        non-linear quantization parameters. Unavailable without sufficient
+        decoded metadata; Profile 7 or an EL track alone does not distinguish
+        these types. Describes the source metadata, not EL composition success.
+
     ``video-frame-info/gop-timecode``
         String with the GOP timecode encoded in the frame.
 
@@ -3705,6 +3718,20 @@ Property list
         Dolby Vision profile and level. May not be available if the container
         does not provide this information.
 
+    ``track-list/N/dolby-vision-config-bl-present``, ``track-list/N/dolby-vision-config-el-present``, ``track-list/N/dolby-vision-config-rpu-present``
+        Boolean BL, EL and RPU declarations from this track's Dolby Vision
+        configuration record. Unavailable when no record is available, even
+        if an authored stream relation provides a profile. These flags do
+        not indicate successful decoding, mapping or enhancement composition.
+
+    ``track-list/N/dolby-vision-group-bl-present``, ``track-list/N/dolby-vision-group-el-present``
+        True on a base track with an explicit Dolby Vision enhancement-layer
+        stream relation. Unavailable otherwise; two ordinary HEVC tracks do
+        not establish this relation. Includes virtual split enhancement tracks
+        and authored disc groups. These describe the overall BL/EL structure,
+        independently of each track's in-band configuration flags, and do not
+        report whether enhancement decoding or composition succeeded.
+
     ``track-list/N/metadata``,
         Works like the ``metadata`` property, but it accesses metadata that is
         set per track/stream instead of global values for the entire file.
